      "body": "# PR type\n- [x] Bug Fix\n- [ ] New Feature\n- [x] Document Updates\n- [ ] More Models or Datasets Support\n\n# PR information\n\nRelated issue: none. Found by code inspection and reproduced with constructed CPU calibration data.\n\nDecision-model calibration fits `fold_head_t[fold]` and `fold_relative[fold]` on records outside `fold`, but then scores that fold with the entries for `1 - fold`. The reported out-of-fold ECE, Brier and NLL therefore use temperatures fitted on the scored records. Index both temperatures by the held-out fold instead.\n\nAdd regression coverage using the real Brier and NLL solvers, soft targets with analytic optimal probabilities, multiple question kinds per record, non-contiguous record IDs, and padded options. Document the existing small-sample fallback in both languages. The production temperatures fitted on all evaluation data and the fallback behavior are unchanged.\n\n## Experiment results\n\n- `OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 MKL_NUM_THREADS=1 .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/general/test_temperature_calibration.py tests/train/test_laya_decision.py tests/train/test_decision_loss.py -q`: **16 passed** on CPU (PyTorch 2.14.0, Python 3.13.15). Both new cases fail against the unmodified upstream callback: in-sample Brier is near zero instead of the analytic held-out value of 0.04.\n- `.venv/bin/python -m pre_commit run --all-files`: all hooks passed. `git diff HEAD --check` and `pip check` passed.\n- A separate constructed `on_train_end` check with a real `JevVerbalizerHead` reports Brier 0.2033 after the fix, matching an independently fitted held-out reference (previously 0.0196). The output and last-checkpoint `scoring_head.json` files are identical before and after the fix and reload successfully. This was a CPU callback experiment, not a full training run or a rerun of the historical documentation benchmarks.\n- Checked all 155 initially open PR titles and complete file lists, relevant closed PRs and the callback history; no competing fix was found. The final refresh contained 152 open PRs and no new PRs or callback overlaps.\n\nAI assistance: OpenAI Codex assisted with code inspection, implementation and validation.\n\n# Checklist\n\n- [x] I have linked the related issue above, if there is one.\n- [ ] I have reviewed and understand every changed line, and I can explain how the change works and why it is correct.\n- [ ] I have run the relevant tests or reproductions locally, and included the commands and results above (if applicable).\n- [ ] I am responsible for the content of this PR, regardless of how it was produced.\n",
