  "files": [
    {
      "additions": 2,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/modelscope/ms-swift/blob/740bf14ae50d9f88b0da3366b8ee22ab7b728edf/docs%2Fsource%2FBestPractices%2FDecision.md",
      "changes": 2,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/modelscope/ms-swift/contents/docs%2Fsource%2FBestPractices%2FDecision.md?ref=740bf14ae50d9f88b0da3366b8ee22ab7b728edf",
      "deletions": 0,
      "filename": "docs/source/BestPractices/Decision.md",
      "patch": "@@ -183,6 +183,8 @@ $$\n \n **报告指标（2-fold 交叉验证）**：为避免\"用拟合数据给自己打分\"的乐观偏差，日志里的 accuracy / ECE / Brier / NLL 是 **out-of-fold** 的——验证 record 按奇偶分两折，每折的温度在对面那折上拟合，再用来给本折打分。注意：**写进 checkpoint 供线上使用的温度仍是用全部验证数据拟合的**（生产估计），CV 只影响日志口径。同一条 record 的多道题总是落在同一折，避免信息泄漏。\n \n+如果不同 record 不足两条，或某个训练半折的题数少于 `SWIFT_CALIBRATION_MIN_ITEMS`，对应指标会回退到使用全部验证数据拟合的温度，因此不属于严格的 out-of-fold 评估。\n+\n ### 日志解读\n \n 训练开始时先输出 base 基线（`on_train_begin`，用出厂/加载温度在验证集上评估，纯报告不写入）：",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/modelscope/ms-swift/raw/740bf14ae50d9f88b0da3366b8ee22ab7b728edf/docs%2Fsource%2FBestPractices%2FDecision.md",
      "sha": "76e0a3ebc4f6f66ca57be721dd5a033df8fa4839",
      "status": "modified"
    },
    {
      "additions": 2,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/modelscope/ms-swift/blob/740bf14ae50d9f88b0da3366b8ee22ab7b728edf/docs%2Fsource_en%2FBestPractices%2FDecision.md",
      "changes": 2,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/modelscope/ms-swift/contents/docs%2Fsource_en%2FBestPractices%2FDecision.md?ref=740bf14ae50d9f88b0da3366b8ee22ab7b728edf",
      "deletions": 0,
      "filename": "docs/source_en/BestPractices/Decision.md",
      "patch": "@@ -157,6 +157,8 @@ $$\n \n **Reported metrics (2-fold cross-validation)**: to avoid the in-sample optimism of scoring the fitted data with the fitted temperature, the accuracy / ECE / Brier / NLL in the logs are **out-of-fold** — eval records are split into two halves by parity, each half's temperature is fitted on the opposite half, and used to score its own half. Note that **the temperature written into the checkpoint is still fitted on ALL eval data** (the production estimate); the CV only affects the reported numbers. All questions of one record always land in the same fold, preventing leakage.\n \n+If there are fewer than two distinct records, or a training half has fewer than `SWIFT_CALIBRATION_MIN_ITEMS` questions, the affected metrics fall back to temperatures fitted on all eval data and are not strictly out-of-fold.\n+\n ### Reading the logs\n \n A base baseline is logged at the start of training (`on_train_begin`, evaluated with the loaded/factory temperatures, report-only):",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/modelscope/ms-swift/raw/740bf14ae50d9f88b0da3366b8ee22ab7b728edf/docs%2Fsource_en%2FBestPractices%2FDecision.md",
      "sha": "2d4993e6873b082241d12a715c662e5c3f5f3e68",
      "status": "modified"
    },
    {
      "additions": 1,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/modelscope/ms-swift/blob/740bf14ae50d9f88b0da3366b8ee22ab7b728edf/swift%2Fcallbacks%2Ftemperature_calibration.py",
      "changes": 3,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/modelscope/ms-swift/contents/swift%2Fcallbacks%2Ftemperature_calibration.py?ref=740bf14ae50d9f88b0da3366b8ee22ab7b728edf",
      "deletions": 2,
      "filename": "swift/callbacks/temperature_calibration.py",
      "patch": "@@ -613,8 +613,7 @@ def _cross_validated_metrics(self, all_items: List[Dict], head_t: float,\n         nlls: List[float] = []\n         for it in all_items:\n             fold = half[it['record_id']]\n-            eval_fold = 1 - fold\n-            t = _clamp_temperature(fold_head_t[eval_fold] * fold_relative[eval_fold].get(it['kind'], 1.0))\n+            t = _clamp_temperature(fold_head_t[fold] * fold_relative[fold].get(it['kind'], 1.0))\n             logit = it['logits']\n             target = it['target']\n             mask = it['mask']",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/modelscope/ms-swift/raw/740bf14ae50d9f88b0da3366b8ee22ab7b728edf/swift%2Fcallbacks%2Ftemperature_calibration.py",
      "sha": "f278ad62c12bdc304dc657d532fa3e1d2efa4b9a",
      "status": "modified"
    },
    {
      "additions": 40,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/modelscope/ms-swift/blob/740bf14ae50d9f88b0da3366b8ee22ab7b728edf/tests%2Fgeneral%2Ftest_temperature_calibration.py",
      "changes": 40,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/modelscope/ms-swift/contents/tests%2Fgeneral%2Ftest_temperature_calibration.py?ref=740bf14ae50d9f88b0da3366b8ee22ab7b728edf",
      "deletions": 0,
      "filename": "tests/general/test_temperature_calibration.py",
      "patch": "@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@\n+# Copyright (c) ModelScope Contributors. All rights reserved.\n+import pytest\n+import torch\n+\n+from swift.callbacks.temperature_calibration import TemperatureCalibrationCallback\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.parametrize('loss_name', ['brier', 'nll'])\n+def test_calibration_metrics_use_held_out_records(loss_name):\n+    callback = TemperatureCalibrationCallback(None, None)\n+    callback.loss_name = loss_name\n+    callback.min_items = 10\n+    items = []\n+    for record in range(20):\n+        for kind in range(3):\n+            items.append({\n+                # Non-contiguous IDs with the same parity: splitting is by record order.\n+                'record_id': 100 + 6 * record,\n+                'kind': kind,\n+                'logits': torch.tensor([2., 0., 100.]),\n+                'target': torch.tensor([.8, .2, 0.] if record % 2 == 0 else [.6, .4, 0.]),\n+                'mask': torch.tensor([True, True, False]),\n+            })\n+\n+    metrics = callback._cross_validated_metrics(items, 1., {})\n+\n+    # Both objectives have an interior optimum matching each half's soft targets.\n+    # Held-out scoring must use the opposite half's probabilities. Scoring the\n+    # fitting half instead would give a near-zero Brier score rather than 0.04.\n+    targets = torch.tensor([[.8, .2], [.6, .4]])\n+    probabilities = targets.flip(0)\n+    expected_brier = (probabilities - targets).square().mean().item()\n+    expected_nll = -(probabilities.log() * targets).mean().item()\n+    expected_ece = (1 - probabilities[:, 0]).mean().item()\n+\n+    assert metrics['accuracy'] == 1.\n+    # Allow the numerical solvers' convergence tolerance around the analytic optimum.\n+    assert metrics['brier'] == pytest.approx(expected_brier, abs=5e-4)\n+    assert metrics['nll'] == pytest.approx(expected_nll, abs=5e-4)\n+    assert metrics['ece'] == pytest.approx(expected_ece, abs=5e-4)",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/modelscope/ms-swift/raw/740bf14ae50d9f88b0da3366b8ee22ab7b728edf/tests%2Fgeneral%2Ftest_temperature_calibration.py",
      "sha": "996f2de7af31596778afe6528b57067025d88902",
      "status": "added"
    }
